    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTall Trees is an exceptional detached dormer residence, combining timeless elegance with outstanding craftsmanship, set amid approximately 0.69 HA (1.7 acres) of beautifully landscaped private gardens and grounds. Enjoying a highly desirable countryside setting, the property offers the perfect balance of privacy and convenience, just minutes from Dublin Airport, Swords Village, and the M1/M2/M50 motorways. An excellent range of sporting and leisure amenities are nearby, including renowned golf clubs, equestrian centres, GAA clubs, and Roganstown Hotel & Country Club.\nBehind its striking Howth stone façade lies a home of immense character and distinction, thoughtfully designed to accommodate modern family living while embracing an active and sporting lifestyle. Meticulously upgraded to the highest standards, no expense has been spared in the presentation, finish, and attention to detail throughout this remarkable residence.\nA magnificent entrance hall sets the tone, featuring vaulted ceiling and dual-aspect windows that flood the space with natural light. Glazed double doors open to a grand reception hall adorned with bespoke wall panelling by Leonard Cabinetmakers and a feature staircase. Stunning Belgian Oak Palazzo engineered flooring throughout the ground floor enhances the sense of luxury and warmth.\nTo the front of the property, the elegant formal living room and adjoining study enjoy views over the sweeping driveway, tennis court, and manicured lawns. A striking dual-aspect wood-burning stove with back-to-back fireplaces creates an inviting focal point.\nAt the heart of the home is a spectacular bespoke kitchen and dining area, handcrafted by Leonard Cabinetmakers and complemented by premium appliances. This impressive space opens into the bright and spacious family room, where large picture windows frame views of the rear gardens and provide access to the extensive patio and Belgian Veranco aluminium and glass enclosure. A practical boot room is conveniently located off the kitchen.\nAdditional ground floor accommodation includes an impressive bar and games room, guest bathroom, sauna, and a large utility room, ensuring every modern convenience is catered for.\nUpstairs, the accommodation is equally impressive, comprising four generously proportioned ensuite bedrooms, including a luxurious principal suite complete with dressing room and elegant ensuite bathroom.\n\nOutside\nApproached by electronic security gates framed by Howth stone pillars and walls, the grounds of Tall Trees are a true sanctuary. They extend to circa 0.69 H/A (1.7 acres) and the winding driveway leads past a tennis court, full-size soccer goal and large fishpond, offering ample secure parking and an electric vehicle charging point.\nThe rear gardens are designed for both relaxation and entertainment, featuring an expansive patio area and a superb Belgian Veranco aluminium and glass enclosure with motorised canopy, infrared heating, and LED lighting. \nFurther outdoor amenities include refurbished outbuildings currently used as a recreation studio with traditional sprung dance floor, table-tennis table, TV area (ideal for video games) and WC facilities, as well as a home gym with a separate WC, a bicycle shed and a garden shed.\nBeautifully mature trees, specimen planting and lawns create a wonderful sense of seclusion, making the gardens a private oasis ideally suited to family life and outdoor pursuits.\n\nOffering an unrivalled combination of luxury, space, privacy, and recreational facilities, Tall Trees is a truly unique family home. \nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate everything this outstanding residence has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.03m x 2.75m\nExtended-height entrance door, feature ceiling with roof lights, dual aspect side windows, Eichholtz lantern, Belgian Oak Palazzo engineered wood floor, double doors (glazed) to Entrance Hall\n\nReception Room - 8.15m x 1.77m\nWall panelling (Leonard Cabinetmakers), feature staircase to upper floor, step down to inner hall\n\nLiving Room - 5.98m x 3.88m\nFormal living room with access to Study. Elegant fireplace with dual aspect wood burning inset stove, Belgian Oak Palazzo engineered floor, distinctive bay window with shutters overlooking front garden, spotlights on ceiling, access to Study\n\nStudy - 3.70m x 3.14m\nFitted bookshelves and cabinets (Leonard Cabinetmakers), Belgian Oak Palazzo engineered wood floor, feature fireplace with dual aspect wood burning stove, picture window to front with shutters and views of front garden\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 10.55m x 3.62m\nStunning bespoke fitted kitchen by Leonard Cabinetmakers with excellent press units. Granite work surfaces, large central Island with 2 x sinks, Sterling Stove (Induction Hob and 4 Ovens), Miele Dishwasher, Fisher & Paykel fridge, built-in Microwave and TV, Eichholtz Lights, Belgian Oak Palazzo wood floor, step down to open plan family area\n\nBoot Room - 1.83m x 1.67m\nExcellent boot room with door to rear\n\nBoiler Room - 1.90m x 1.50m\nAdjacent to Boot Room and accessed by a separate entrance\n\nFamily Area - 6.00m x 3.80m\nCombined with the Kitchen/Dining Room this wonderful open area is the centre of family life. Feature vaulted ceiling with roof lights, Belgian Oak Palazzo wood floor, large picture window (fitted with wired motorised blinds) overlooking the rear garden, double patio doors to an extensive patio area with Belgian Veranco aluminium and glass\n\nInner hall - 4.23m x 0.98m\nSteps from Entrance Hall, Belgian Oak Palazzo wood floor, feature wall panelling (Leonard Cabinetmakers)\n\nUtility Room - 6.52m x 1.86m\nSpanish Marble floor, excellent built in press units, sink unit, washing machine and dryer, spotlights on ceiling, door to rear\n\nGuest bathroom - 2.51m x 1.53m\nDecorative wall panelling, Spanish Marble Tiling, wc, whb, large shower\n\nBar / Snug - 8.05m x 3.90m\nStained Oak floorboards, Patio doors to front garden, Feature raised fireplace with inset wood burning stove on Howth Stone base, Bespoke Bar with Pub Grade Cooler System, Beer Taps and Snooker Table. Workstation ideal for WFH. Picture windows (shutters) to front\n\nSauna Room - 4.38m x 3.64m\nBelgian Oak Palazzo wood floor, patio door to rear garden (shutters), spotlights on ceiling, Sauna\n\nUPSTAIRS - \n\n\nLanding (1) - 2.30m x 1.91m\nSpacious landing area with wall panelling. Access to floored attic with ample storage space\n\nLanding (2) - 6.52m x 0.98m\nSpacious landing area with wall panelling\n\nPrinciple Suite (comprising of) - \n\n\n- Entrance - 3.30m x 1.20m\nPrivacy enhancing space connecting Principal Bedroom, Dressing Room and Ensuite\n\n- Bedroom - 5.00m x 3.71m\nPeriod Fireplace with gas fire insert (chimney sealed and fire disconnected, now for decorative purposes only), air conditioning, attractive window detail to front, cloaks closet\n\n- Dressing Room - 4.10m x 1.88m\nWalk in wardrobe area with built in dress unit and shutter window\n\n- Principal Ensuite - 4.48m x 2.00m\nStunning Ensuite comprising bath, large rain shower, His n Hers whb, wc, bidet, heated towel rail (x2), Spanish Marble tiling and feature wall panelling\n\nBedroom 2 - 6.14m x 2.84m\nPicture windows with shutters overlooking the front garden, built in study desk and shelf unit, steps to Ensuite\n\nEnsuite - 3.00m x 1.90m\nElegant Ensuite with Travertine Tiling, large rain shower, wc, whb, heated towel rail (x2), Velux window\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.90m x 4.10m\nL Shaped room with dual aspect windows (shutters), built in study desk and shelf unit\n\nEnsuite - 2.27m x 1.75m\nTiled large rain shower, wc, whb, attractive wall panelling, heated towel rail, Velux window\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.00m x 2.70m + 1.77m x 0.98m\nSplit Level Bedroom with large window (shutters)\n\nEnsuite - 2.40m x 1.70m\nBespoke fitted bath with a separate shower tap and shower screen, elegant tiling, wc, whb, heated towel rail, wall panelling, shutter windows\n\nHotpress - 1.89m x 1.44m\n\n\nOUTBUILDINGS - \n\n\nRecreation Studio (comprising of) - \nMulti-purpose area with traditional sprung dance floor and mirror wall, industrial style exposed steel and timber beams, theatre-inspired lighting, powerful wired speakers, picture floor to ceiling windows overlooking the rear garden and house. Central Heating (separate boiler), Heat Recovery Ventilation system (by ProAir), WC\n\n- Entrance - 2.40m x 2.15m\n\n\n- Table tennis / TV area - 7.70m x 6.35m\n\n\n- Dance floor area - 4.40m x 4.40m\n\n\n- WC - 2.20m x 1.20m\n\n\nGym Area (comprising of) - \n\n\n- Gym (soft flooring) - 7.10m x 3.15m\n\n\n- Storage - 5.70m x 1.15m\n\n\n- WC - 1.40m x 1.15m\n\n\nBicycle shed - 3.48m x 3.22m\n\n\nGarden Shed - 5.00m x 3.60m\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Stunning Detached Dormer Residence </li><li>Magnificent gardens extending to circa 1.7 Acre </li><li>Belgian Oak Palazzo engineered wood floor (Ground)</li><li>Superb bespoke fitted kitchen and panelling by Leonard Cabinetmakers</li><li>Top quality appliances </li><li>Spanish marble in Utility, Downstairs Bathroom, Principal Ensuite</li><li>Belgian Veranco Aluminium Patio Enclosure with Motorised Canopy and Infrared Heaters</li><li>Heat Recovery Ventilation systems (by ProAir) in the House and Recreation Studio</li><li>Air conditioning in Principal Bedroom</li><li>High End Lighting</li><li>Chappée Floréal cast iron radiators</li><li>Two Wood-burning Inset Stoves with external air supply </li><li>Recreation Studio with sprung dance floor (built using bending woven wooden battens)</li><li>Gym</li><li>Tennis Court, soccer area with a full-size goal, basketball board, table tennis</li><li>Short drive from Dublin Airport </li><li>Convenient to M50 / M1 / M2 Motorway</ul>"
